title: SalemDay0Start
---
<<declare $playerName="player">>
<<gatherVars>>
The campus café was a hot spot for students during lunch time,
but now as it's only morning, it was calm. The soft jazz music
set the atmosphere, and as you entered, you saw only one worker
on the floor. She was humming to yourself, a small smile on her
face as she dried some glasses.
She heard the chimes of windpipes clashing together in sync and
she looked over to you, and now you could see her face. She had
a dreamy look in her face, as if she were lost in thought.

Salem: "Hiii, Welcome to Portal and Prose,"

You looked at her, before approaching the counter. She was a
soft looking person, soft smile adorning her face and wavy
lavender hair. There was a welcoming energy emitting from her,
and it drew you in almost immediately

-> Ask for her name
    <<incRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump AskName>>
->Make small talk
    <<jump MakeTalk>>
->Immediately ask her to participate in the essays
    <<decRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump AskForParticipant>>
===

title: AskName
---

You: "Hi… How’re you?"

The server blinked and smiled happily, as if no one had bothered
to ask her that today. The thought made you feel a little bad,
and she had enthusiastically giggled.

Salem: "Im good, thank you so much!"

The simple question made her so happy, it made you surprised.

<<jump SinceYouNever>>
===

title: MakeTalk
---
Your fingers drummed on the counter, the server looking
expectantly at you. The cafe was vacant other than you and her
which seemed sort of peculiar.

You: "So... Are you the only one working?"

Your attempt of making small talk seemed to fall on deaf ears as
the server blinked and nodded slowly, seemingly confused. You
got nervous, in hindsight, asking if someone is alone is...sort
of concerning.

Salem: "Well yes I am. There are more but they're on their
breaks now. Right now is our quietest hours so that's why I'm
alone."

You nodded and hummed. Huh, you supposed in actuality she didn't
mind the question. Thank god.

<<jump SinceYouNever>>
===

title:AskForParticipant
---
Not wasting any time, you drummed your fingers on the counter.

You: "Hi my name is Y/n. I need some volunteers for my last
essay in Philosophy, and I was wondering if you'd be interested
in being one."

The server looked at you, face contorting in an awkward smile as
she looked away. Oh...maybe you came off too strong.

Salem: "Are you here to order...?"

She quickly diverted the conversation...and now you felt awkward

<<jump SinceYouNever>>
===

title: SinceYouNever
---
Since you never came to this cafe before, you didn't know
exactly what was nice. With too much choice your eyes glided to
the server who was waiting for what you wanted.

You: "Hmm...what would you recommend?"

For a second the server's eyes glimmered. She stopped what she
was doing, humming in thought before she sat down the glass she
was drying.

Salem: "Ooooo, I'd recommend the caramel macchiato and the
fudge brownie."

Smiling, you nodded and ordered it, and she nodded with a happy
smile. She seemed to be very friendly, this could be a chance to
know more about her.

-> Compliment her hair
    <<incRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump ComplimentHair>>
-> Ask about her job
    <<jump AskAboutJob>>
-> Stay silent
    <<decRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump StaySilent>>
===

title: ComplimentHair
---
You found their hair striking, the colour was very pretty, and
before you knew it your mouth opened.

You: "Your hair is really pretty."

The server beamed happily at you, her fingers twirling her hair
before giggling. You slowly blinked, she really liked the
compliment.

Salem: "Thank you!!"

She hummed happily as she made your coffee and placed your
brownie on your tray, and your initial nervousness disappeared.
Her natural bright energy clouded whatever anxious thoughts you
had; she seemed naturally bright and kind.

You: "It's no bother."

Still she beamed and giggled, eyes curving and looking like
crescent moons.

<<jump FoodArrives>>
===

title: AskAboutJob
---
You: "So... What's it like being a cafe barista?"

The server brewed your coffee and hummed as if to say she's
listening. She turned around with the freshly made coffee in
hand, placing it on a tray.

Salem: "Hmm... It's nice. I do like it... sometimes it's
stressful but that's like all jobs."

She takes some tongs, taking one muffin from the collection and
setting it on a plate, moving it on the tray too.

<<jump FoodArrives>>
===

title: StaySilent
---
You decided against it. It seemed sort of early to ask about
herself. Wouldn’t it be creepy? She placed the coffee on a tray,
and then she placed the brownie down as well. She finally looked
back at you, and with a soft, gentle smile tilted her head at
your staring.

<<jump FoodArrives>>
===

title: FoodArrives
---
Salem: "Here's your order, dear. That will be 11.99."

You tapped your phone to the card reader, and she went back to
tidying things up as you sat on an empty chair.

-> Ask her about herself
    <<incRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump AskAboutSalem>>
-> Ask about the weather
    <<jump AskAboutWeather>>
-> Eat your food
    <<decRelationship "Salem" 1>>
    <<jump EatYourFood>>
===

title: AskAboutSalem
---
You: "So..."

The server looked at you while she worked. Looking up, she was
currently wiping down the counter even when it still looked
spotless.

You: "Are you in uni?"

Her wiping slowed before she looked back at the counter.

Salem: "I am actually!"

She sounded very happy as she spoke.

Salem: "Im a student here, so its convenient that I work here,"

She ended what she said with a giggle.

From there you asked her more questions about herself. She
seemed more than happy to share more information about herself
to you, and her eyes seemed more relaxed the more you spoke.

Eventually, your cup became empty and your brownie was in your
stomach, and you were nice and full.

<<jump LookingBackAtHer>>
===

title: AskAboutWeather
---
You sat down at an empty chair, placing your tray of goods on
the table. The atmosphere was suddenly quiet and you felt that
you should say something.

You: "Nice weather we’re having huh?"

You said it to pass the time, biting into the brownie. The
server looked up from what she was doing, which was wiping down
the counter, and she blinked in what seemed like confusion.

You also blinked back, wondering why she wasn’t saying anything,
before looking out the window. It was raining. Hard. Ah…so
that’s why.

Salem: "It’s raining…"

She said it bluntly, and you sighed and cringed. Yeah…you
already knew.

You: "Nice for uh the plants,"

You added despite the embarrassment, and she just smiled and
nodded. So much for making it less awkward, you just made it
worse.

<<jump LookingBackAtHer>>
===

title: EatYourFood
---
You sat down at an empty chair, placing your tray of goods on
the table. The atmosphere was suddenly quiet and you felt that
you should say something.

You thought about what to say and…nothing. You had an inkling
you’d ruin the atmosphere so you sat there silently and ate
your food.

<<jump LookingBackAtHer>>
===

title: LookingBackAtHer
---
Looking back at her as you sat in your chair, you contemplated
whether or not to ask her to be apart of your candidates. There
was no limits on who you could ask, so you decided why not.

You approached the counter again after you were done with your
food and she saw you waiting. Washing her hands and drying them
off, she came over, showing you a kind smile once more.

Salem: "Hi dear, did you want to order more?"

She asked, and you shook your head.

You: "Hi, I was just wondering,"

You started after a weird period of silence. She stood up
straighter at that, turning fully to face you.

You: "My name is Y/n. I need some volunteers for my last essay
in Philosophy, and I was wondering if you'd be interested in
being one,"

She tilted her head, blinking at you as she considered your
words.

Salem: "Okay! I'll join,"

You smiled happily and gave her the first question you needed,
explaining what it was for. She nodded eagerly, and you bid her
a goodbye.

She seemed nice.
===